# clause-runtime-driver — Design

Compiler-side dispatcher. Owns the dylib handle; routes calls
through the ABI.

## Scope

- `Runtime` struct wrapping the dylib handle.
- Dylib loading via libloading with version validation.
- Per-entry-point safe wrappers over the `extern "C"` declarations.
- Error mapping from `AbiDiagnostic` to clause-ir::Diagnostic.
- Integration with clause-schedule's pass DAG (macro-expansion
  pass + generative-expansion pass).

## Non-scope

- ABI contract (clause-runtime-abi).
- Runtime logic (clause-runtime-zig).
- Dylib bundling / distribution (separate round).

## Dependencies

- `clause-ir`, `clause-runtime-abi`, `clause-schedule`.
- libloading for dlopen/dlsym.

## Provisional module layout

- `runtime.rs` — Runtime struct + lifecycle.
- `invoke.rs` — macro invocation wrapper.
- `scratch.rs` — scratch-eval wrapper.
- `generative.rs` — generative-expansion wrapper.
- `error.rs` — AbiDiagnostic → Diagnostic conversion.

